brief:
Decide the trust boundaries of a published flake and of an agent evaluating one: nixConfig, accept-flake-config, tokens, secrets, substituters and daemons.
Rows: M-H-01..09 (nix-topic-map.md). Map conflict 7 is the direction to confirm or overturn.
Fetch: nix.dev/manual/nix/2.35/command-ref/conf-file (accept-flake-config, access-tokens, trusted-users, trusted-substituters); nix3-flake (nixConfig); NixOS/nix issues 9649, 6752, 9788 and 9885; github.com/NixOS/nix/security/advisories (GHSA-g3g9-5vj6-r3gj, GHSA-6fjr-mq49-mm2c, CVE-2026-39860); wiki.nixos.org/wiki/Flakes (secrets); NixOS/nixpkgs PR 300028; DeterminateSystems/flake-checker README (check-owner).
Test against:
- the 11 nixConfig-bearing exemplars (nix-audit/exemplar-flake-shape.md section 6);
- nix-community/nix-vscode-extensions@329083cd32e0:flake.nix:46-50 (extra-trusted-substituters, hydra.iohk.io);
- numtide/llm-agents.nix@efb10f28f724:flake.nix:3-7 (allow-import-from-derivation in nixConfig) and its AGENTS.md:13, which tells agents to pass --accept-flake-config;
- ipetkov/crane@73b980519cef:.github/workflows/test.yml:104 (CI passes --accept-flake-config);
- cachix/cachix@3349ce74ba77:README.md:90 (an install line with --accept-flake-config).
Cite, do not re-derive: nixConfig.warn-dirty is inert without accept-flake-config (nix-inputs.md); registry data interpolated into a builder is a build-time injection (NIX-GEN-20); Authorization is never forwarded across hosts (NIX-GEN-10); --no-write-lock-file and a full SHA apply when evaluating a flake you do not own (NIX-INP-12, map E8).
Plant in fixtures/trust-boundaries/:
- a flake whose nixConfig carries extra-substituters, a post-build-hook and allow-import-from-derivation, evaluated as the untrusted single user with and without accept-flake-config; record prompts, warnings and effects;
- Q12's allowlist check (nix eval --impure --json --expr over (import ./flake.nix).nixConfig), watched red and green;
- a secret read with builtins.readFile that lands in the store; show the world-readable path;
- access-tokens supplied through NIX_CONFIG versus a committed nix.conf;
- an FOD with impureEnvVars and a pinned hash (M-H-06).
Reconcile the CVE-2026-39860 fixed versions with NIX-GATE-16's computed floor (2.31.5) and NIX-GATE-13's install_url pin.
Decide: the nixConfig allowlist and its severity; the accept-flake-config rule for READMEs, CI and agent instructions; token and secret placement; the safe flags for evaluating an untrusted flake; daemon version floors for CI and self-hosted builders. Every rule needs a check watched red.
Env: Nix only via /home/mherwig/.cache/research-lang/nix-tools/run.sh (CppNix 2.35.2, nixpkgs 26.11pre 8d5d2709, jq, flake-checker 0.2.15). Wrap each call in timeout 300. run.sh uses bwrap with WAL on, so parallel dives are fine. If timeout 60 run.sh nix --version fails, write ENVIRONMENT FAULT first and stop all Nix work. Fixtures go under /home/mherwig/.cache/research-lang/nix-tools/fixtures/ (never /tmp); git init -q and git add -A before any eval. Exemplars are read-only (SHAs in nix-fetch.log). Pipe grep and find through rtk proxy. Run every check verbatim: a directory operand, one -e per alternative, quoted --include globs, xargs -r, no placeholders. Each check goes red on the violation and green on the twin, and its write-up states what empty output means, the versions, and cold or warm store.
